    "faq_giiP7V": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_FpjCdQ": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is LAMININE safe for animal consumption?",
            "content": "<p>While LAMININE wasn’t originally developed for animals, extensive testing and feedback from pet owners and veterinarians have confirmed it's safe for pet consumption. There have been no reported adverse reactions in animals, and many veterinarians recommend LAMININE for pets. However, as with human consumption, if you have any specific concerns or questions about whether your pet should take LAMININE, consult your veterinarian before giving LAMININE to your pet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_y6QpXy": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What does “human-grade” ingredients mean?",
            "content": "<p>LAMININE is made with human-grade ingredients, meaning the high-quality ingredients we use meet the same rigorous standards and testing as those intended for human consumption. Produced in a cGMP, NSF, and FDA-approved lab in the USA, LAMININE is non-GMO and holds a clean label and halal certification. LAMININE was originally developed for humans, but vets and pet parents find it works just as well for animals of all kinds. The results have been incredible, and we want you to see the same results in your pet!</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_Ff7PgR": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How does LAMININE work to increase the years I have with my pet?",
            "content": "<p>LAMININE doesn’t just mask the problems that come with aging, it helps reverse and slow down the signs of aging. Our formula is created using FGF-2, a powerful growth factor that plays a vital role promoting telomere lengthening. Telomeres are the caps that protect the ends of DNA, and shorter telomeres lead to a higher risk of age-related symptoms.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_ENtwg9": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How can animals benefit from taking LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>Pets taking LAMININE can experience decreased joint pain, improved mobility, more energy, and accelerated healing. It also supports healthier skin, coat, hearing, and eye health. LAMININE works to keep your pet feeling its best by working to extend telomere length and prevent damaged DNA. Slower signs of aging mean your pet can stick around for longer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_hXJpey": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the suggested LAMININE for different animals, such as cats, dogs, and horses?",
            "content": "<p>The recommended LAMININE serving varies by animal size. For dogs and cats up to 40 pounds, give half to one capsule daily during meal time. Animals weighing 40 to 80 pounds should receive two capsules daily, and those between 80 to 100 pounds, up to three capsules daily. Horses typically require about four capsules daily.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_hHrUJU": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will the dosage you recommend be too much for my pet?",
            "content": "<p>The suggested dosage is safe for your pet and is based on the recommendations of veterinary professionals. LAMININE is formulated to be safe for pets across different sizes, breeds, and species. While the suggested dosage guidelines are designed to be safe, we understand individual pets may have a unique health history or special needs and sensitivities. If you’re unsure of the dosage your pet needs, it’s always best to consult with your vet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_YErTHm": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When should pets be given LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>LAMININE should be given to pets during their meals to ensure optimal absorption and minimize digestive discomfort. Consult your veterinarian for specific recommendations tailored to your pet's dietary schedule and health needs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_KttgTP": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long does it typically take to see results after starting LAMININE for pets?",
            "content": "<p>Every pet is different, so some may see results faster than others. Results from LAMININE can typically be noticed within a few days to weeks. Your pet may show increased energy and improved mobility within the first four weeks. More significant and long-term benefits can often be noticed within four to eight weeks of consistent use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_k3Fq49": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can LAMININE benefit pets with joint discomfort?",
            "content": "<p>Definitely! It’s one of the things LAMININE does best. By supplying essential amino acids and growth factors, LAMININE helps reduce inflammation and repair joint tissues. Regular use can significantly enhance the quality of life for pets suffering from joint issues.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_c9hjYY": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can LAMININE be used as a preventive measure, or is it only for existing conditions?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, many pet owners use LAMININE to prevent signs of aging before they even start. By giving your pet LAMININE you can proactively support their long-term well-being, helping them maintain their youthful energy and active lifestyle.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
